※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7013 LANG_MACRO_HOLE_UNKNOWN

※ A hole in a template is filled with what the hole of that name matched, so one
※ the pattern does not have can never be filled.  It is reported where the rule is
※ written rather than at whatever invocation first reaches it, which is the one
※ thing about a rule that does not wait for a caller.

macro wrong:
    ⌜$x⌝ → ⌜$y + $y⌝

